{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/2/context.json","@id":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/manifest/4ce6f23f-7682-41f5-8e46-639a8ba9570f.json","@type":"sc:Manifest","label":"Bodleian Library MS. Laud Lat. 6","description":"Glossed biblical books","metadata":[{"label":"Homepage","value":"<span><a href=\"https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/objects/4ce6f23f-7682-41f5-8e46-639a8ba9570f/\">View on Digital Bodleian</a></span>"},{"label":"Catalogue Description","value":"<a href=\"https://medieval.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/manuscript_7635\">Full catalogue record in Catalogue of Western Medieval Manuscripts in Oxford Libraries</a>"},{"label":"Title","value":"Glossed biblical books"},{"label":"Shelfmark","value":"Bodleian Library MS. Laud Lat. 6"},{"label":"Former Owner","value":"Laud, William, 1573-1645"},{"label":"Language","value":"Latin"},{"label":"Date Statement","value":"1200–1210"},{"label":"Place of Origin","value":"France"},{"label":"Description","value":"Composite manuscript: Part A: ff. 1-24. Part B: ff. 25-109. Part C: ff. 110-119."},{"label":"Contents","value":"Acts, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 1-24). Proverbs, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 25r-71r). Ecclesiastes, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 72r-84v). Wisdom, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 85r-109v). Song of Songs, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 110r-117r). Daniel, with glossa ordinaria (ff. 117v-119v)."},{"label":"Materials","value":"Parchment"},{"label":"Extent","value":"ff. ii + 119 + 1 (medieval endleaf, f. 120) + i leaves, foliated i-ii, 1-121."},{"label":"Binding","value":"Brown tanned calf over laminated pulpboard for Abp. Laud, 1637–1639."},{"label":"Provenance","value":"All parts probably bound together early on: they share an annotating hand. All parts probably at Würzburg, Domstift St Kilian, in the thirteenth century. Part B is annotated by a thirteenth-century hand also found in MSS. Laud Lat. 41, 42, 98, 115. William Laud, 1573-1645, by 1636 (f. 1r). Part of his third donation to the Bodleian, sent 28 June 1639."},{"label":"Record Origin","value":"This description is abbreviated from Daniela Mairhofer, Medieval Manuscripts from Würzburg in the Bodleian Library, Oxford: A Descriptive Catalogue (Oxford, 2014), pp. 156-62. For purposes of scholarly citation, reference to the printed catalogue is requested."},{"label":"Collection","value":"Western Medieval Manuscripts"},{"label":"Digitization Project","value":"Manuscripts from German-Speaking Lands: A Polonsky Foundation Digitization Project (2018-2021)"},{"label":"Record Created","value":"2019-02-01T14:09:15+00:00"},{"label":"Holding Institution","value":"Bodleian Libraries, University of Oxford"},{"label":"Digitization Sponsor","value":"<span>The Polonsky Foundation<br/><img src=\"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/image/058aac61-1416-4c92-9be4-fc7af5faaf20/full/!255,255/0/default.jpg\" alt=\"The Polonsky Foundation logo\"/></span>"}],"navDate":"1200-01-01T00:00:00Z","rendering":{"@id":"https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/objects/4ce6f23f-7682-41f5-8e46-639a8ba9570f/","label":"View on Digital Bodleian","format":"text/html"},"attribution":"<span>Photo: © Bodleian Libraries, University of Oxford. Terms of use: <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/\">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>. For more information, please see <a href=\"https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/terms/\">https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/terms/</a></span>","logo":{"@id":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/image/f27e28db-0b08-4f16-9bdf-3565f591fb71/full/256,/0/default.jpg","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg","service":{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json","profile":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/level1.json","@id":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/image/f27e28db-0b08-4f16-9bdf-3565f591fb71"}},"thumbnail":{"@id":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/image/6b96e910-a7f6-4dae-80a2-ec736a583f43/full/256,/0/default.jpg","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg","service":{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json","p